{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3336","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3336","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3336\",\"parent_revision\":\"99ee42e17229156c50dd5a76386b34ca90e21002\",\"root_revision\":\"5d6450b0fd59001dadc9cc76f54ede5e88190b4ba408bdb82972ac8b49189641\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe root cause behind #3329's deletion, generalized: `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` re-explained MCP tool parameters and return shapes in hand-written prose that the tool's own docstring/`Field(description=...)` annotations already stated \u2014 and that duplicate was structurally guaranteed to drift, because FastMCP regenerates the live tool schema from the code every server start, while a prose copy in a skill file changes only when someone remembers to edit it. That mechanism is what produced the deleted skill's \\\"12 tools\\\" heading against 28 real ones, a dead storage-format claim, and a broken `fastmcp` invocation example.\\n\\nConfirmed during #3329 this isn't unique to that one skill: `plugins/development-harness/README.md`'s \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table has the identical shape (filed separately as #3335).\\n\\nGoal: audit other `dh:*` skills for the same pattern \u2014 prose that restates an MCP tool's parameters, return fields, or behavior, checkable live against the tool's actual schema via `ToolSearch`. Where found: delete the restatement from the skill, and if a genuine content gap exists, add it to the tool's own docstring instead (verified in #3329 to be the correct destination \u2014 it's literally the schema the agent is shown when deciding how to call the tool, a stronger and self-maintaining hook that a skill-file restatement can never be).\\n\\nUser-provided context: see #3329 for the full investigation this generalizes from, including three concrete examples where this exact check (comparing a doc's claim against the live `ToolSearch` schema) revealed the doc was either already redundant or actively wrong.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:43:13.508056Z</sub>\\n\\n## Claim 1: artifact_register enum coverage in create-artifact/SKILL.md\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (documentation incomplete and contradictory instruction)\\n\\nclaim: Skill file lists only 7 of 10 live `artifact_type` enum values, missing `dispatch-plan` and `audit-report`. Skill also explicitly instructs agents never to pass `artifact_type=\\\"task-plan\\\"` even though `task-plan` is a valid enum member on the live schema.\\n\\nevidence:\\n- Live `artifact_register` schema enum contains 10 values: feature-context, architect, task-plan, T0-baseline, TN-verification, codebase-analysis, code-review, research, dispatch-plan, audit-report\\n- Skill file table (lines 61-68) documents only 7 types: feature-context, codebase-analysis, code-review, architect, T0-baseline, TN-verification, research (omits dispatch-plan, audit-report, and task-plan from table)\\n- Skill file section \\\"task-plan\\\" (lines 128-132) redirects users away from `artifact_register`: \\\"Task plans live exclusively in SAM plan storage. Create them with `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan(...)` and retrieve them with `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan(...)`\\\" \u2014 contradicting the valid schema enum value\\n\\nsource:\\n- Live: `artifact_register` enum parameter (ToolSearch)\\n- Skill: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/create-artifact/SKILL.md lines 128-132\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Claim 2: backlog_update milestone parameter in groom-milestone/SKILL.md\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (documentation claims unsupported feature)\\n\\nclaim: Skill file (line 89) states `backlog_update(selector, ...)` can \\\"assign milestone,\\\" but live `backlog_update` schema has no `milestone` parameter.\\n\\nevidence:\\n- Skill file line 89 lists tool as: \\\"`backlog_update(selector, ...)` \u2014 assign milestone, update item fields\\\"\\n- Live `backlog_update` schema parameters: content, description, entry_id, plan, reason, replace_section, section, selector, status, title, verified \u2014 no `milestone` parameter present\\n- Schema is silent on milestone assignment through backlog_update\\n\\nsource:\\n- Live: `backlog_update` parameters (ToolSearch)\\n- Skill: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md line 89\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Claim 3: #-prefixed beads nanoid selector format in implement-feature/SKILL.md\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (claim supported through schema pattern inference)\\n\\nclaim: Comment (lines 142-143) states \\\"#\\\"-prefixed beads nanoids fail to resolve as a `selector` parameter: \\\"No '#' prefix: find_item resolves a bare GitHub number or a bare beads nanoid, but a '#'-prefixed nanoid resolves neither.\\\"\\n\\nevidence:\\n- Skill file comment (lines 142-143): \\\"No '#' prefix: find_item resolves a bare GitHub number or a bare beads nanoid, but a '#'-prefixed nanoid resolves neither.\\\"\\n- Live `backlog_groom` selector parameter description lists valid formats: \\\"GitHub issue URL, #N, bare number, or title substring, or beads nanoid (e.g. bd-a3f8)\\\"\\n- Schema separates formats: `#N` (for numbers only) and `beads nanoid (e.g. bd-a3f8)` (shown without # prefix)\\n- The schema example `bd-a3f8` (not `#bd-a3f8`) supports the skill's claim that # does not pair with beads nanoids\\n\\nsource:\\n- Live: `backlog_groom` selector parameter description (ToolSearch)\\n- Skill: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md lines 142-143\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:47:54.073340Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: GAP\\nclaim: `backlog_groom` returns `mark_groomed_skipped`/`mark_groomed_skip_reason` fields\\nevidence: Tool schema docstring at server.py:2615-2617 states \\\"Returns: Dict with groomed item title, synced status, and output messages/warnings.\\\" However, the actual implementation at operations.py:3776-3777 shows these fields ARE returned by groom_item() when mark_groomed=True and the re-parsed item lookup fails. Lines shown: `result[\\\"mark_groomed_skipped\\\"] = True` and `result[\\\"mark_groomed_skip_reason\\\"] = f\\\"Item '{selector}' not found in re-parsed backlog\\\"`.\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:3771-3789 (groom_item function), plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2615-2617 (tool schema docstring)\\n\\n---\\n\\nverdict: STALE\\nclaim: `backlog_resolve` response contains a `milestone` field\\nevidence: Tool schema docstring at server.py:2416-2418 states \\\"Returns: Dict with resolved item title, summary, and output messages/warnings.\\\" The actual implementation at operations.py:3386 returns `{\\\"title\\\": item.title, \\\"resolved\\\": True, \\\"summary\\\": summary, **out.to_dict()}`. No `milestone` field is present or constructed in the resolve_item() function. This claim is fabricated and does not appear in the actual response payload.\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:3306-3386 (resolve_item function), plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2416-2418 (tool schema docstring)\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T09:48:18.754462Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: chore: Audit other dh:* skills for hand-written MCP tool documentation that duplicates and drifts from live tool schemas\\nDate: 2026-08-30\\nGoal: Find and fix (or file) other dh:* skills that restate MCP tool parameters/return shapes in prose that drifts from the live ToolSearch schema, the same mechanism that caused #3329's \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current inventory of dh:* skill directories under plugins/development-harness/skills/ (post-#3329 deletion count) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Which of those skills (SKILL.md + bundled references/agents files) contain prose naming or de