skipped field duplication** (finalize.md + groomer-output-validation.md) \u2014 same claim in two files, coordination risk if behavior changes\\n2. **backlog_resolve milestone field** (close/start.md) \u2014 needs source verification before deciding if field actually exists\\n\\nBoth are contained and ready for delegation to Wave 2's planning phase.\\n\\n### Readiness Conclusion\\n\\n**Item Status: READY FOR PLANNING**\\n\\n- All five RT-ICA conditions are satisfied (AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE)\\n- Fact-Check provided expected drift patterns with clear evidence\\n- Impact Radius established scope boundary (42 files, 2 scope-expansion items)\\n- No missing information blocks progress to task decomposition\\n- Scope is proportionate to P1 priority (audit + documentation corrections + docstring relocation)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:44:22.608350Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: recurring-pattern\\n\\n**Rationale**: The same mechanism (hand-written MCP tool parameters/return shapes in skill prose drifting from live ToolSearch schemas) has appeared 2+ times: #3329 (deleted dh:backlog skill with \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect), #3335 (README.md Core backlog tools table), plus 3+ confirmed new instances in Wave 0 research (create-artifact/SKILL.md, groom-milestone/SKILL.md, implement-feature/SKILL.md). This is structural drift, not a one-off bug.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: RCA via backlog history keyword search (MCP tool documentation drift patterns, hand-written schema restatement, skill doc staleness) across resolved items to measure frequency. Secondary signal: cross-reference #1113 (agent name reference audit), #1161 (section access pattern incompleteness), #1672 (doc-drift-auditor scope gap) \u2014 all reflect the same root cause: documentation maintaining its own copy of source-of-truth data instead of referencing it.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Skills and README files that restate MCP tool parameters \u2192 instead, delete prose duplicates and r