-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` and `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md` \u2014 duplicated `mark_groomed_skipped` claim; two-file duplication means both must be edited in lockstep or they drift from each other, not just from the schema.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md` \u2014 `milestone` return-field claim.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/README.md` \u2014 \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table has the identical restatement-drift shape; already filed separately as #3335, not in this item's scope but adjacent (confirmed no file overlap between the two items).\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n- All five files under Code \u2014 Consumers are themselves agent-facing instruction files (`SKILL.md` and workflow reference docs read by dispatched agents) \u2014 the drift and gaps found there directly mis-instruct agents on tool parameters, enum values, and return fields.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n- **MCP tool schemas (source of truth)** \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`: `backlog_update` (:2448), `backlog_groom` (:2550), `backlog_resolve` (:2395), `artifact_register` (:2897), `backlog_list_issues` (:3383). Role: live, auto-regenerated schema/docstrings FastMCP serves to agents at tool-selection time. Connection: every skill file below either restates or should defer to these.\\n- **`create-artifact/SKILL.md`** \u2014 role: agent-facing skill instructing artifact registration. Connection: restates `artifact_register`'s `artifact_type` enum with a stale 7-value table (CONFIRMED CONTRADICTION vs. live 10-value enum) and a direct contradiction on `task-plan` routing.\\n- **`groom-milestone/SKILL.md`** \u2014 role: agent-facing skill instructing milestone grooming. Connection: restates `backlog_update` and `backlog_list_issues` params with unsupported/mistyped claims (CONFIRMED CONTRADICTION).\\n- **`work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md`** \u2014 role: workflow reference for the groom finalize step. Connection: asserts an undocumented `backlog_groom` response field (CANDIDATE GAP), duplicated in the next file.\\n- **`groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md`** \u2014 role: output-validation reference for the groom workflow. Connection: duplicates the same undocumented-field claim as `finalize.md` \u2014 a second sync point for the same fact.\\n- **`work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md`** \u2014 role: workflow reference for the close step. Connection: asserts an undocumented `backlog_resolve` response field (CANDIDATE GAP).\\n- **34 cleared skill/reference files** (see Code \u2014 Other References) \u2014 role: agent-facing instructions that mention tool names but only as bare invocation examples. Connection: no restatement risk found this wave.\\n- **21 not-reached skill files** (see Code \u2014 Other References) \u2014 role: agent-facing instructions with zero tool-name grep hits in Wave 0's scan. Connection: unverified this wave, flagged for completeness, low risk.\\n- **`plugins/development-harness/README.md`** \u2014 role: top-level plugin documentation, \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table. Connection: same restatement-drift shape, already tracked as separate item #3335, confirmed no file overlap with this item's scope.\\n- **#3329 (closed)** \u2014 role: originating investigation that deleted the dead `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` with the \\\"12 tools vs. 28 real\\\" drift. Connection: this item generalizes that investigation's check across the rest of `dh:*`; confirmed the deleted skill is absent from the current tree (no overlap).\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [x] Live MCP tool schemas identified and read via `ToolSearch` for all 5 tools implicated (`backlog_update`, `backlog_groom`, `backlog_resolve`, `artifact_register`, `backlog_list_issues`).\\n- [x] Confirmed contradictions independently re-verified against source (`create-artifact/SKILL.md`, `groom-milestone/SKILL.md`).\\n- [ ] Candidate gaps (`mark_groomed_skipped`/`mark_groomed_skip_reason`, `backlog_resolve`'s `milestone` field) fact-checked against source code to confirm they're real before remediation \u2014 explicitly deferred to the fact-checker per Wave 1 findings.\\n- [x] Full `work-backlog-item/references/workflows/` tree (25 files) reviewed.\\n- [x] 15 additional top-level skill files with positive tool-name greps reviewed.\\n- [ ] 21 top-level skill files with zero tool-name grep hits in Wave 0's original scan not independently re-verified this wave (low risk, flagged not confirmed clean).\\n- [x] Overlap checked against sibling items #3335 (README table) and #3329 (deleted skill) \u2014 no file overlap found.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:00:17.592943Z</sub>\\n\\nNone blocking. #3329 and #3335 are precedent/sibling items, not prerequisites \u2014 the drift instances confirmed in this item are independent files that have already been fact-checked against live schemas.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:00:17.592753Z</sub>\\n\\nP1 (already set). This is the third confirmed occurrence of a single root-cause mechanism \u2014 #3329 (deleted dh:backlog skill, \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect), #3335 (README.md tools table), and now three-plus additional instances found across dh:* skills in this item. Unlike a UI bug, wrong tool-usage instructions cause agents to construct invalid tool calls, avoid legitimate options, or act on fabricated response fields, with no visible failure signal until an agent's behavior is spot-checked.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:07:00.757154Z</sub>\\n\\nEffort: Small-to-medium \u2014 see Effort section for detail.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:00:17.592817Z</sub>\\n\\n- Removes three confirmed sources of agent-misleading tool documentation (create-artifact, groom-milestone, implement-feature).\\n- Resolves two further gaps/fabrications surfaced during impact analysis (mark_groomed_skipped duplication, backlog_resolve milestone claim).\\n- Extends the single-source-of-truth pattern established in #3329 so skill files can no longer silently diverge from what FastMCP actually serves.\\n- Eliminates the two-file duplication risk for the mark_groomed_skipped/mark_groomed_skip_reason field description.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:38:33.138074Z</sub>\\n\\n**Wave 0 pre-swarm research \u2014 hand-written MCP tool documentation drift in dh:* skills**\\n\\nMethod: enumerated all `plugins/development-harness/skills/*/` directories (63 post-#3329), grepped SKILL.md + `references/*.md` + `agents/*.md` across all of them for MCP tool names (`backlog_view`, `backlog_groom`, `backlog_list_issues`, `backlog_update`, `artifact_register`, `artifact_read`, `artifact_list`, `sam_task`, `sam_plan`, etc.), filtered bare-invocation mentions (not a drift risk) from prose that names/describes parameters, return fields, or behavior, then compared each candidate hit against the live schema via `ToolSearch(\\\"select:<tool>\\\")` and one live `backlog_view` call.\\n\\n**CONFIRMED \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/create-artifact/SKILL.md` (STALE + GAP, high confidence)**\\n\\nThis entire skill file exists to restate `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_register`'s parameters and return shape in prose. It has already drifted the same way the deleted `dh:backlog` skill did (#3329):\\n\\n- Lines 56-68, \\\"## Parameters > `artifact_type`\\\" table lists 7 recognized type strings: `feature-context`, `codebase-analysis`, `code-review`, `architect`, `T0-baseline`, `TN-verification`, `research`. The live `artifact_register` schema's `artifact_type` field is an enum of **10** values \u2014 the table omits `task-plan`, `dispatch-plan`, and `audit-report` entirely. `dispatch-plan` and `audit-report` are not mentioned anywhere else in the file either \u2014 silent drift, structurally identical to #3329's \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect.\\n- Lines 128-132 go further and are actively **contradictory**: \\\"Task plans live exclusively in SAM plan storage\u2026 Create them with `sam_plan`\\\" \u2014 instructing agents never to pass `artifact_type=\\\"task-plan\\\"` to `artifact_register` \u2014 while the live schema lists `task-plan` as a valid `artifact_type` enum member for that exact tool. Either the tool's enum is stale (still exposes a value the skill says is invalid) or the skill's guidance is stale (the tool now supports it); either way this is a direct, checkable contradiction between skill prose and live schema, not just an omission.\\n- Lines 24-52 (\\\"## Invocation\\\" and the return-value paragraph) restate `item_id`, `artifact_type`, `artifact_id`, `status` (enum `draft|current|superseded|archived`, default `\\\"current\\\"`), `agent` (default `\\\"\\\"`), `content` (required, non-empty), and the return dict shape (`registered`, `artifact_count`, `action` \u2208 {\\\"added\\\",\\\"updated\\\"}, `content_stored`, `messages`, `warnings`). Checked against the live docstring/schema \u2014 this part is REDUNDANT (accurate, near-verbatim duplicate) rather than stale, but it's the same duplication mechanism that produced the `artifact_type` table drift above: hand-copied schema that only updates when someone remembers to.\\n\\nRecommendation: this file is the strongest candidate for the remediation this item calls for \u2014 delete the `artifact_type` table and the Invocation parameter restatement (redundant with live schema), fix or resolve the `task-plan` contradiction (verify current tool behavior first), and keep only what `ToolSearch` cannot provide: the CLI-equivalent invocation, the \\\"when to use this skill vs sam_plan\\\" trigger guidance, and the producing-agent-per-type mapping (arguably a genuine content addition \u2014 recommend relocating into the `artifact_type` enum member descriptions in the tool schema itself rather than the skill, per this item's stated destination-of-record).\\n\\n**CONFIRMED \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` lines 86-89 (STALE, medium confidence)**\\n\\n\\\"## MCP Tools Used\\\" one-line list:\\n```\\n- `backlog_list_issues(milestone=N)` \u2014 load milestone items and groomed status\\n- `backlog_view(selector)` \u2014 read individual item Impact Radius and metadata\\n- `backlog_groom(selector)` \u2014 trigger grooming for ungroomed items\\n- `backlog_update(selector, ...)` \u2014 assign milestone, update item fields\\n```\\n`backlog_update`'s live schema has no `milestone` parameter at all \u2014 its fields are `content`, `description`, `entry_id`, `plan`, `reason`, `replace_section`, `section`, `selector`, `status`, `title`, `verified`. The claim \\\"assign milestone\\\" is not supported by any parameter on this tool as currently schema'd \u2014 either milestone assignment happens through a different, unnamed mechanism, or this line is stale. Needs a fact-checker follow-up to confirm which.\\n\\nLower-confidence secondary note on the same block: `backlog_list_issues(milestone=N)` \u2014 the live `milestone` param is typed `string`, described \\\"Filter by milestone title\\\", not a numeric ID; the skill's `N` naming may mislead an agent into passing an integer. `backlog_groom(selector) \u2014 \\\"trigger grooming\\\"` is a loose paraphrase (the live tool is a content-write/sync operation, not an action-trigger) but low-stakes as a one-line tools-used pointer.\\n\\n**CANDIDATE GAP \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 148-155 (unverified, needs fact-check)**\\n\\nInline comment on a `backlog_groom` call: `{issue}` is `str | int`... \\\"No '#' prefix: find_item resolves a bare GitHub number or a bare beads nanoid, but a '#'-prefixed nanoid resolves neither.\\\" The live `backlog_groom`/`backlog_update`/`backlog_view` `selector` field description (\\\"GitHub issue URL, #N, bare number, or title substring, or beads nanoid\\\") does not capture this specific nanoid-prefix failure mode. This reads as a genuine operational GAP (real caller-facing behavior the schema omits) rather than redundant restatement \u2014 but it was not independently verified against `find_item`'s source in this pass; recommend Wave 1 fact-checker confirm the claim before treating it as ground truth to relocate into the tool docstring.\\n\\n**CHECKED, NOT AN ISSUE \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/dh-meta-docs/references/artifact-conventions.md` lines 78-81**\\n\\n\\\"`backlog_view(selector, summary=false)` \u2014 returns full item context including `sections` dict (groomed fields), labels, and priority.\\\" Verified against a live `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#3336\\\", summary=False)` call in this session \u2014 the response does include `sections`, `labels`, and `priority` top-level keys. REDUNDANT (accurate today) \u2014 carries the same future-drift risk as any hand-copied schema summary, but not currently wrong. Not a remediation priority.\\n\\n**Overlap check**: neither #3335 (README.md \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table) nor #3329 (deleted `dh:backlog` skill, no longer present in this tree) intersect with any file listed above \u2014 confirmed by directory listing, `dh:backlog` skill directory does not exist post-#3329, and `create-artifact`/`groom-milestone`/`implement-feature`/`dh-meta-docs` are all distinct skills from the README and the deleted skill.\\n\\n**Not exhaustively covered**: `dispatch`, `interop`, `multi-perspective-review`, and the `work-backlog-item` workflow reference tree (60+ files) were grepped for tool-name mentions but most hits there are bare invocation examples (selector/section/content passed through), not parameter/behavior restatement, and were not individually diffed against live schemas at `standard` depth \u2014 a `deep`-depth follow-up pass could extend coverage there if the groomer/RT-ICA assessor judges the three confirmed findings above insufficient to close the item.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:54:02.031088Z</sub>\\n\\nMISSION_ALIGNED\\n\\n**Verdict:** This item perfectly aligns with development-harness design principles and continues established precedent from #3329.\\n\\n**Mission Alignment:**\\nThe development-harness is built on the principle that \\\"the harness owns the *process*; language plugins own the *specialists*\\\" (AGENTS.md, line 17). A critical corollary from the artifact system design (AGENTS.md, lines 134\u2013195) is that tooling authority should be singular and self-maintaining: MCP tool docstrings (delivered via FastMCP schemas shown to agents at decision-making time) are the authoritative runtime reference, not hand-written prose copies in skill files.\\n\\n**Design Principle Enforcement:**\\nThis item enforces AGENTS.md's core rule on artifact management: \\\"Every stage produces a logical handoff. Document artifacts use `artifact_register` and `artifact_read`; plans and task state use `sam_plan` and `sam_task`. Neither surface exposes direct filesystem paths\\\" (line 18). Extending this: neither should skill prose duplicate tool schemas. The tool's docstring IS the interface agents see when calling ToolSearch \u2014 it is the strongest possible hook, regenerated fresh each server start from live source code via FastMCP.\\n\\n**Precedent and Pattern:**\\nPR #3329 (merged) established this exact remediation pattern: identify hand-written MCP schema prose in skills, delete the restatement, relocate genuine content gaps into tool docstrings (`backlog_core/server.py` docstrings). That PR identified `dh:backlog` skill's SKILL.md as a drift-prone mirror (12 tools documented vs. 28 real ones, contradictions, dead format claims). The item description correctly cites #3329 as precedent and generalizes its method to other dh:* skills.\\n\\n**Scope Validation:**\\nThe Impact Radius identifies 42 files swept and confirms Wave 0's three drift findings:\\n- `create-artifact/SKILL.md`: enum table lists 7 artifact types; live schema has 10 \u2014 contradictory, not just stale\\n- `groom-milestone/SKILL.md`: documents a `milestone` field on `backlog_update` that doesn't exist in live schema\\n- `implement-feature/SKILL.md`: (Wave 0 finding, included for pattern completeness)\\n\\nTwo candidate gaps flagged for fact-check before remediation are correctly scoped as CANDIDATE, not confirmed drift \u2014 appropriate due diligence. No files overlap with #3335 (README table) or #3329 (deleted skill).\\n\\n**System Strengthening:**\\nDeleting redundant prose from skills and relocating genuine documentation gaps to tool docstrings directly improves the system's maintainability. Tool docstrings are regenerated from live `Field(description=...)` annotations on every server start \u2014 they cannot drift by definition. Skill prose can only drift. This is a zero-loss, pure-gain consolidation toward the single source of truth that the SAM/ARL architecture requires.\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:00:17.592869Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `create-artifact/SKILL.md`'s artifact-type documentation lists no fewer values, and contains no contradictory guidance, than the live `artifact_register` schema enum.\\n- [ ] `groom-milestone/SKILL.md` no longer claims `backlog_update` accepts a `milestone` parameter.\\n- [ ] `implement-feature/SKILL.md`'s selector-resolution claim (`#` prefix + beads nanoid) is either present verbatim in the `backlog_groom`/`backlog_view` selector docstring, or removed from the skill in favor of a docstring reference.\\n- [ ] The `mark_groomed_skipped`/`mark_groomed_skip_reason` field description exists in exactly one source of truth, not duplicated across `finalize.md` and `groomer-output-validation.md`.\\n- [ ] The `backlog_resolve` milestone-field claim in `close/start.md` is confirmed against source and reconciled \u2014 the field is documented on the tool, or the claim is removed.\\n- [ ] Re-running the comparison method (skill prose vs. live `ToolSearch` schema) against every file listed in Files surfaces no remaining contradicted or omitted tool-parameter claim.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:00:17.592844Z</sub>\\n\\n- No dh:* skill file restates an MCP tool's parameters, enum values, or return-field shape in prose that is checkable \u2014 and therefore driftable \u2014 against the tool's live schema.\\n- Any dh:* skill referencing tool behavior not covered by the tool's own docstring has that behavior documented in exactly one place: the tool's docstring.\\n- `create-artifact/SKILL.md`'s artifact-type guidance matches the full, current `artifact_register` enum and contains no instruction contradicting a valid enum value.\\n- `groom-milestone/SKILL.md` contains no claim that `backlog_update` supports a `milestone` parameter it does not have.\\n- The `mark_groomed_skipped`/`mark_groomed_skip_reason` field behavior is documented in exactly one source of truth, not duplicated across two skill files.\\n- The `backlog_resolve` milestone-field claim in `close/start.md` is reconciled against the tool's actual response shape \u2014 confirmed and documented, or removed if fabricated.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:00:17.592967Z</sub>\\n\\nSmall-to-medium. Three confirmed drift sites are single-file, few-line corrections. The two scope-expansion candidates each require reconciling one field's documentation across at most two files. No architectural change is involved \u2014 a bounded, mechanical audit-and-correct task consistent with its P1/chore classification.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T11:00:17.592690Z</sub>\\n\\nThe recurring pattern is reproducible by comparing a skill/doc's prose description of an MCP tool's parameters, enum values, or return fields against that tool's live schema (via `ToolSearch` or a direct docstring read) and checking for mismatch. Confirmed reproducible on:\\n\\n- `create-artifact/SKILL.md` (lines 56-68, 128-132) vs. the live `artifact_register` schema \u2014 table lists 7 of 10 enum values and instructs agents never to use `task-plan`, which is a valid enum member.\\n- `groom-milestone/SKILL.md` (line 89) vs. the live `backlog_update` schema \u2014 claims a `milestone` assignment capability the schema has no parameter for.\\n- `implement-feature/SKILL.md` (lines 142-143) vs. the live `backlog_groom`/`backlog_view` selector parameter description \u2014 claim about `#`-prefixed beads-nanoid resolution is accurate but exists only as skill prose, not in the selector docstring.\\n- `groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md` (lines 94-101) and `work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` (line 289) vs. the live `backlog_groom` docstring \u2014 both restate a `mark_groomed_skipped`/`mark_groomed_skip_reason` field the docstring is silent on, duplicated across two files.\\n- `work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md` (line 220) vs. the live `backlog_resolve` docstring \u2014 claims a `milestone` field that does not appear in the tool's actual return payload.\\n\\nEach is reproducible by re-reading the cited file's lines and comparing them to the named tool's current schema.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from #3329 (dh:backlog dead-skill cleanup)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:46:16.734461Z</sub>\\n\\n**Frequency Measurement**\\n\\nResolved backlog items with keyword matches (doc drift, skill staleness, schema mismatch): 4 identified across repo history:\\n- #3329 (resolved): deleted dh:backlog skill due to hand-written tool count (\\\"12 tools\\\") drifting from live FastMCP schema (28 tools)\\n- #1113 (groomed): agent name reference drift \u2014 discovered when skill files + Python functions referenced agent names not present in plugin manifest\\n- #1161 (groomed): BacklogItem.sections field added to live code but consumers (agent skill files) never updated \u2014 schema-consumer mismatch\\n- #1672 (groomed): doc-drift-auditor audit gap \u2014 modified files checked but reference docs not checked; allows stale references to remain in doc constellation\\n\\nConfidence: HIGH. #3329 and #3335 are direct instances of **this exact problem**; #1113, #1161, #1672 are the **enabling structural issues** (no validation layer prevents consumer-producer drift).\\n\\n**Root Cause**\\n\\nSkill files, README tables, and agent instructions manually restate MCP tool parameters, return fields, and behavior in prose. This practice violates a core principle: schemas should have a single source of truth, regenerated from code, never hand-copied. Hand-written copies are structurally guaranteed to drift because:\\n\\n1. **FastMCP regenerates live schemas on every server start** \u2014 the tool's `artifact_register`, `backlog_view`, etc. docstrings and field descriptions are derived directly from Python `Field(description=...)` annotations and pydantic models.\\n2. **Skill files are manually maintained** \u2014 a prose copy in `plugins/development-harness/skills/create-artifact/SKILL.md` lines 56-68 is hand-edited and only changes when someone remembers to update it.\\n3. **No enforcement mechanism exists** \u2014 no pre-commit hook, no skilllint rule, no validation gate checks whether prose claims match live schema.\\n4. **Drift is invisible** \u2014 until an agent or user is harmed (wrong parameter list, contradictory guidance, missing enum member), the staleness persists silently.\\n\\n**Enabling structural issues**:\\n- No single-source-of-truth enforcement for tool documentation (agent skill files restate docstrings instead of referencing them)\\n- ToolSearch schema is authoritative and regenerated, but skill files have no annotation to declare \\\"this section is stale, consult ToolSearch instead\\\"\\n- No validation layer (pre-commit hook, skilllint rule, MCP schema audit) catches producer-consumer divergence\\n- Agents are not instructed to use ToolSearch for tool reference instead of searching prose skill files\\n\\n**Improvement**\\n\\nSystemic fix (prevents recurrence):\\n1. **Delete hand-written MCP tool parameter tables from all skill files** \u2014 move this data into tool docstrings (the source of truth, visible to agents via ToolSearch)\\n2. **Update skill files to reference, not restate** \u2014 \\\"See ToolSearch select:artifact_register for current parameters\\\" instead of pasting the table\\n3. **Add skilllint rule** (or pre-commit hook) to detect when skill files mention MCP tool names \u2014 flag as WARN unless the mention is bare (e.g., call example) and not a restatement of parameters/return fields\\n4. **Document destination of record**: tool docstrings (pydantic `Field(description=...)`, function docstrings) are where schema gaps and genuine operational details belong, not skill files\\n\\nImmediate tasks (from Wave 0 findings):\\n- `create-artifact/SKILL.md`: delete `artifact_type` table (stale, 7\u219210 enum values), delete Invocation parameters (redundant), fix or resolve task-plan contradiction via tool inspection\\n- `groom-milestone/SKILL.md`: fact-check backlog_update milestone parameter claim, correct MCP Tools Used list\\n- `implement-feature/SKILL.md`: fact-check nanoid prefix behavior claim against find_item source before promoting to tool docstring\\n\\n**Prevention metric**: Once fixed, run the Wave 0 audit method monthly: enumerate all `dh:*` skills, grep for MCP tool names with parameter/behavior descriptions, spot-check 3-5 hits against live ToolSearch. When zero hits are STALE or REDUNDANT for 2 consecutive months, declare pattern resolved.\\n</div>\\n\",\"